# The ollama CLI is only a client: `ollama list` hanging with "timed out
# waiting for server to start" means nothing is listening on :11434.

# To start the server (menu-bar app; installed via the ollama-app cask):
open -a Ollama

# Or run it in the foreground instead (logs in the terminal, ctrl-c to stop):
ollama serve

# To check it's up and see what's available:
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/models | jq -r '.data[].id'
ollama list

# To get a model / free the RAM it holds after use:
ollama pull <model>
ollama stop <model>

# To stop the server: quit the menu-bar app (Ollama icon -> Quit).
